{%- comment -%}
  latest-news-EM — the three most recent articles from a blog.

  1 use: index. The filename keeps its odd suffix because the type name is
  frozen — `latest-news-EM` is what the template asks for. Do not tidy it.

  Setting IDs kept: `heading`, `bg_color`, `blog`.

  ONE SETTING CHANGED
  `bg_color` was a free colour picker holding #f4f4f4 — a grey that belongs to
  no part of the FYE palette, and the reason this band looked like a different
  website. It is now a palette choice, defaulting to ivory (the brand's warm
  ground, and the nearest thing to what #f4f4f4 was reaching for). A saved hex
  is ignored and falls back to ivory.

  No block types: the articles come from the blog, so there is nothing to
  configure per item. If an article has no image the card drops the image and
  keeps its text rather than showing a grey box.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign band = s.bg_color
  unless band == 'ivory' or band == 'white' or band == 'mist'
    assign band = 'ivory'
  endunless
  assign src = blogs[s.blog]
-%}

<section class="news band band--{{ band }}" data-screen-label="Latest news">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="news__head">
      {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="news__heading">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if src != blank and src.url != blank -%}
        <a class="link news__all" href="{{ src.url }}">All articles</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if src.articles_count > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Four articles: the newest as a lead with a large image, then three
        stacked beside it with thumbnails. Matching live — my first pass was
        three equal cards, which has no focal point and takes more height for
        fewer articles.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="news__grid">
        {%- for article in src.articles limit: 4 -%}
          <li class="news__item{% if forloop.first %} news__item--lead{% endif %}">
            <a class="news__link" href="{{ article.url }}">
              {%- if article.image != blank -%}
                <span class="news__img">
                  {{ article.image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag:
                     loading: 'lazy', widths: '300,500,700,900',
                     sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 33vw',
                     alt: article.title }}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
              <span class="news__words">
                <time class="eyebrow" datetime="{{ article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">
                  {{ article.published_at | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}
                </time>
                <span class="news__title">{{ article.title }}</span>
                {%- if article.excerpt_or_content != blank -%}
                  <span class="news__excerpt">{{ article.excerpt_or_content | strip_html | truncatewords: 22 }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%} No blog chosen, or an empty one: say so in the editor
        rather than rendering an empty band with a heading. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        <p class="lead">Choose a blog in this section's settings.</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .news__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s6);
  margin-bottom: var(--s9);
}
/* Lead article left, three stacked right. The lead spans both rows of its
   own column; the rest fill the second column in order. */
.fye .news__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--s6) var(--s10);
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}
.fye .news__item { margin: 0; }
.fye .news__item--lead { grid-row: span 3; }

.fye .news__link { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); }
.fye .news__img { display: block; overflow: hidden; }
.fye .news__img :where(img) {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
  object-fit: cover;
  transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

/* The three stacked ones are a thumbnail beside the headline, not a card. */
.fye .news__item:not(.news__item--lead) .news__link {
  flex-direction: row-reverse;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s5);
  padding-bottom: var(--s5);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}
.fye .news__item:not(.news__item--lead) .news__img { flex: 0 0 96px; }
.fye .news__item:not(.news__item--lead) .news__img :where(img) { aspect-ratio: 1; }
.fye .news__item:not(.news__item--lead) .news__excerpt { display: none; }
.fye .news__item:not(.news__item--lead) .news__title { font-size: var(--fs-small); }
.fye .news__link:hover .news__img :where(img) { transform: scale(1.03); }
.fye .news__words { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s2); }
.fye .news__title {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-h2);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .news__link:hover .news__title { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .news__excerpt { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--ink-soft); }

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .news__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s6); }
  .fye .news__item--lead { grid-row: auto; }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .news__head { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--s3); margin-bottom: var(--s7); }
  .fye .news__item:not(.news__item--lead) .news__img { flex-basis: 72px; }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .fye .news__link:hover .news__img :where(img) { transform: none; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Latest news",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Latest news" },
    { "type": "blog", "id": "blog", "label": "Blog" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "bg_color", "label": "Background", "default": "ivory",
      "options": [
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Ivory" },
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "mist",  "label": "Mist" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Latest news" }]
}
{% endschema %}
